&lt;p&gt;The New York Times is looking for an Analyst to join the Data and Insights Group (DIG).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Data and Insights Group (DIG), you will join a large community of talented analysts who partner with Product, Engineering, Design, Marketing, Strategy, Finance and PMO teams across the business. The ideal candidate will be curious and a collaborative team player. They are someone who understands the value of contribution to a greater whole and the importance of analytic delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate data-driven insights, champion them and drive them into action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain centralized reporting dashboards and automated reports to expand access to data and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write SQL to build pipelines and analyze large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run A/B tests, deliver test analysis and insights and advise on future tests and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise business stakeholders on areas of opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience working with data analytics or data science teams to deliver reporting, analysis and insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and experience working with relational databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one additional scripting language like R or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data visualization and presenting insights from data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset and sense of curiosity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience working in big data environments such as BigQuery or AWS, querying 10M+ rows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience working in dbt or other data transformation or scheduling tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience with version control (Github, code review)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience applying statistical methods to business problems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with A/B testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
