&lt;div class=&quot;WNHJ&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;labeledImage.LOCATION--uid38&quot; class=&quot;WE-Y WMXY WBAB WF0Y&quot; data-automation-id=&quot;responsiveMonikerInput&quot; data-metadata-id=&quot;labeledImage.LOCATION&quot; data-uxi-form-item-child-list-index=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;WJ-Y&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/mission-and-values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;mission&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; of The New York Times is to seek the truth and help people understand the world. That means independent journalism is at the heart of all we do as a company. It’s why we have a world-renowned newsroom that sends journalists to report on the ground from nearly 160 countries. It’s why we focus deeply on how our readers will experience our journalism, from print to audio to a world-class digital and app destination. And it’s why our business strategy centers on making journalism so good that it’s worth paying for.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The New York Times creates original, quality journalism in many forms, from the daily paper to&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;The Daily&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;podcast. Our live events play an important role in this mission, connecting readers to the story and to each other. From flagship convenings like DealBook and Climate Forward to immersive gatherings like Hard Fork Live,&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;New York Times&lt;/em&gt; events intrigue, inform and inspire in equal measure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role for an accomplished creative who can translate the value of world-class journalism into powerful design experiences. You will help bring New York Times journalism to life and create compelling environments for a portfolio of public events and experiences. You will lead creative work that defines both individual events and the overall audience experience across our events portfolio. As part of a cross-disciplinary team, you will shape how audiences experience these moments across every touchpoint, from physical stages to digital screens to marketing assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our New York City headquarters and requires regular in-office attendance three days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategic visual development and art direction for our portfolio of public events and experiences, demonstrating expert knowledge of spatial design, environmental graphics, wayfinding, audience journeys, live audience engagement, and meticulous physical execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the creative lifecycle of each event—from naming and foundational identity to marketing campaigns, live production, and post-event storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thoughtfully integrate the design of sponsor support into revenue-generating events, balancing&amp;nbsp;business objectives&amp;nbsp;with an audience experience that reflects the values of our journalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Art direct video interstitials and live screen graphics, working closely with our Senior Writer for Events to merge narrative outlines with visual storytelling, and collaborating with editors and motion designers to create work that defines the event experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across editorial, events, and marketing to secure resources, navigate live-event production challenges, and steward relationships between editorial priorities and advertising&amp;nbsp;objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the thoughtful documentation of our events, working with photo editors to capture high-quality visual assets that extend the life of the experience and support future programming and partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor&amp;nbsp;a design team dedicated to event projects,&amp;nbsp;cultivating&amp;nbsp;an environment of high-quality execution,&amp;nbsp;continuous&amp;nbsp;learning, and diverse perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate support and understanding of our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/company/mission-and-values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;value of journalistic independence&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and a&amp;nbsp;strong&amp;nbsp;commitment to our mission to seek the truth and help people understand the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will report to the Creative Director for Culture, Communications and Live Experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of hands-on experience&amp;nbsp;in brand identity, spatial and experiential design, environmental graphics, and live-event production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for physical environments, including signage systems, audience wayfinding, and large-scale event graphics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A versatile design portfolio showcasing an experience with layout, typography, and experience handling high-profile editorial content and designing around newsmakers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong conceptual understanding of motion design and the ability to think in and direct motion, with considerable experience collaborating with external motion design studios or internal teams to execute graphics for event screens, presentations, and digital platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with video production workflows and experience directing editors, motion designers, and video teams on larger-scale event productions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency across contemporary design tools (Figma, Adobe Creative Suite) and presentation software (Google Slides), with a&amp;nbsp;strong&amp;nbsp;understanding of motion workflows and social publishing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.A., B.S., B.F.A. or M.F.A.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of&amp;nbsp;effective&amp;nbsp;people management, including creating&amp;nbsp;robust&amp;nbsp;development plans, delivering&amp;nbsp;actionable&amp;nbsp;feedback, and&amp;nbsp;fostering&amp;nbsp;an environment of trust and respect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high bar of accountability and the ability to navigate the demands of live-event production&amp;nbsp;under tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine&amp;nbsp;passion for&amp;nbsp;journalism and a deep curiosity about our work and company—we hope you enjoy&amp;nbsp;reading, watching, and listening&amp;nbsp;to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Compensation and Benefits&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For roles in the U.S., dependent on your role, you may be eligible for variable pay, such as an annual bonus and restricted stock. Benefits may include medical, dental and vision benefits, Flexible Spending Accounts (F.S.A.s), a company-matching 401(k) plan, employee stock purchase plan, paid vacation, paid sick days, paid parental leave, tuition reimbursement and professional development programs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For roles outside of the U.S., information on benefits will be provided during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
