&lt;p&gt;The Creative&amp;nbsp; Production, TBrand Intern is responsible for working with the creative producers across photo, video and audio&amp;nbsp; in the management and production of executions for T Brand Studio, including: vendor bidding and coordination, casting outreach, pre-production logistics, and potentially on-set assistance. The Creative Production, TBrand Intern will also be responsible for working with Business Affairs on the upfront contracting of our vendors as well as any clearance and licensing elements required for creative programs. The Creative Production, TBrand Intern will ensure the strategic alignment of output and ensure it aligns with client objectives. This role will report directly to the Associate Director (Video)Creative Production, T Brand Studio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Senior Creative Producers on assigned programs, staying in lock-step on both creative and logistical aspects of the project.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and/or lead pre-production tasks like vendor &amp;amp; talent outreach/communication, casting, pre-interviews, director’s treatments and any releases needed for shooting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the video, audio and photo production team to clearly communicate project schedules, deliverables and daily/weekly deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess project needs and efficiently identify actionable next steps, with advice from Senior Video Producers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend NYC-based shoots, at the discretion of producers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the management of each project&#39;s budget to include securing estimates, confirmation of deliverables, invoice approval and payment while maintaining budget tracker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compiling and distributing all project details to internal and external resources. This may include securing all required paperwork, such as call creative briefs, creative treatments, shot lists, talent/location releases, contractor paperwork, deal memos, brand guidelines, permits, insurance certificates, post delivery schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;During post-production, collaborate with the Post Producer and BA to ensure all third party logos or rights are cleared for use.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As needed, adept at editing together social cuts or teasers for video programs and internal needs. (Internal work includes but is not limited to T Brand sizzle, promotional reels, award submission videos, etc…)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to take on stretch assignments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate support and understanding of &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/mission-and-values/&quot;&gt;our value of journalistic independence&lt;/a&gt; and a strong commitment to our mission to seek the truth and help people understand the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
