&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The New York Times is seeking a Director of Engineering within the Games Mission. This role involves leading feature engineering teams to deliver exceptional player experience and contribute to business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the VP, Games Engineering and collaborate with Product, Production, Design, and Data partners to develop features that create new value for players, ensuring they remain engaged and subscribed to our products. As a subscription-first company, we are committed to offering high-quality, delightful products, and Games are crucial to our vision of becoming the leading subscription destination for digital puzzles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is vital for building high-quality software and fostering effective engineering teams focused on business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage multiple teams of engineers across iOS, Android, Web and Backend to build new value for players, help players understand value and enable them to create accounts or subscribe and stay&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a line of sight to north star metrics and goals of the Games mission, ensuring that staff understand their purpose and deliverables&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coordinate with other technology teams across Games and other missions to create the right solutions, manage expectations, and keep strategies aligned&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coach and develop engineers and 3+ engineering managers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create an inclusive team culture, recruit for, and retain extraordinary engineering talent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be a thought leader in coming up with long term technical strategy tightly coupled with business needs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrate support and understanding of our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/company/mission-and-values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;value of journalistic independence&lt;/a&gt; and a strong commitment to our mission to seek the truth and help people understand the world&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience leading cross-functional teams, especially in building complex web and mobile products&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2+ years of experience managing engineering managers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1+ years of experience closely managing iOS or Android engineers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven strategic technical leadership and an ability to make sound technical decisions across complex initiatives&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience navigating complex product organizations and balancing diverse stakeholder requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with fostering healthy feedback environments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated track record of inspiring, coaching, and developing high-performing engineering leaders and teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity operating in a high-pressure, fast-paced environment, bringing clarity and sound judgment as priorities evolve&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior engineering experience in the gaming industry&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
