&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analytics Data Products (ADP) is an enablement team in the Data Platform mission. We support Product Engineering teams across The Times in creating, operating, and stewarding data products by providing onboarding workflows, developer experience, modeling expertise, and data-lifecycle standards. We also build shared behavioral data products, such as Pageviews, Sessions, and client-side Interactions, so core reader behaviors can be measured consistently across missions and standalone experiences. Mission teams remain accountable for their domain data while we work alongside them as a forward-deployed team to help them onboard and publish. You will report to the Senior Director of Data Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our New York City headquarters. You can expect to come into the office 3+ days/week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop, and lead a high-performing engineering team, fostering a culture of collaboration, innovation, and high productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own developer experience and tooling (onboarding, CLI, templates, validation, automation) and define and track success metrics such as producer adoption and data reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee roadmap execution, architectural guidance, technical decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain budgets, forecasts and a cost attribution model for your team&#39;s cloud solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers and stakeholders to define requirements and manage change while systematically retiring legacy systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain budgets, forecasts and a cost attribution model for your team&#39;s cloud solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate support and understanding of our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/company/mission-and-values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;value of journalistic independence&lt;/a&gt; and a strong commitment to our mission to seek the truth and help people understand the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of formal people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years building and supporting production data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing or leading technical teams with diverse skill sets and backgrounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience enabling successful collaborations across engineering teams and have a knack for bringing engineers together to achieve shared goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to jump in as needed to assist technically with code reviews, design discussions, and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using SQL to transform data and a working knowledge of at least one of: Python, Java or Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of relational, columnar, and key-value storage technologies as well as data modeling for analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for the Times&#39; mission and desire to join us at a moment in history where our data has the power to transform every aspect of creation and practice of journalism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building developer tooling, onboarding workflows, or internal platforms that other engineering teams adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed systems and event-driven architectures and event instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading migrations or retiring legacy systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
