&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wirecutter’s newsroom relies on our publishing platform to write, edit, and share the recommendations our readers trust. As a Product Manager Intern on the Publishing Platform team, you’ll join the team building and improving those tools and storytelling experiences. You’ll contribute to active product work alongside product, design, and engineering, and your work will support tools and experiences for our editorial colleagues and our audiences. Depending on team priorities, your work may support different parts of the publishing platform. You’ll report directly to the Director of Product Management for the Publishing Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our internship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The duration is 10 weeks long, starting on June 7, 2027.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The rate of pay for this role is $40.00 per hour.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interns work 40 hours per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a hybrid role based in New York City.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to active product work:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the team on real platform work, such as researching a problem, shaping requirements, or evaluating options, with guidance from your manager and teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understand the people we build for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Join conversations with editors and other stakeholders to learn how they work, where the friction is, and what a better workflow looks like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help organize and prioritize opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Collect and structure ideas and requests so the team can prioritize them using established frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use data and research to inform decisions:&lt;/strong&gt; Combine qualitative feedback with existing data to help frame problems and suggest how to test ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communicate clearly:&lt;/strong&gt; Write concise updates, briefs, and other messages, adapting them for a range of audiences, from engineering colleagues to cross-functional partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn how the platform works:&lt;/strong&gt; Build a working understanding of the technologies behind our publishing tools and how engineers assess feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn how a product team works:&lt;/strong&gt; Take part in planning, design reviews, and demos, and build working relationships across a cross-functional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curiosity &lt;/strong&gt;about how publishing and content tools work, how technology supports journalism, and how audiences experience Wirecutter’s journalism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong written and verbal communication&lt;/strong&gt;, including the ability to explain complex ideas simply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort asking clarifying questions&lt;/strong&gt; and learning quickly in unfamiliar territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An analytical mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; you like using evidence to make a case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with using AI tools&lt;/strong&gt; in your day-to-day work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior internship, project, or coursework experience in product, design, data, or journalism. No product management experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
