&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role, Mission or Department Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Android Developer to join our mobile platform engineering team building games experiences for our flagship New York Times Games App. You&#39;ll help design features that delight our customers, and build capabilities and building blocks to ensure our team in delivery. You&#39;ll help shape technical direction while raising the bar for performance, accessibility, and code quality. Working with product, design, and engineering partners, you&#39;ll turn player needs into thoughtful experiences and help the team deliver and improve them at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NYT Games is a collaborative team that values inclusion, diversity and personal growth. We combine product development with a world-class suite of puzzles including beloved titles such as the NYT Crossword, Spelling Bee, Connections, Crossplay and Wordle. Come help us on our journey to grow a world-class mobile platform, as we continue delivering delightful experiences to millions daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our New York City headquarters. You can typically expect to come into the office 3+ days/week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and build scalable, maintainable, and features using Kotlin and modern Android frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech Lead projects and contribute to app architectural decisions, code review, technical roadmap and delivery estimations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product, PMO, design, data, QA, and other engineers to guide product development and translate our requirements into technical specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a technical guide to junior and mid-level developers, encouraging skill growth and adopting developer tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote best standards in Android development, and engage with the community of Android developers at the Times&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate support and understanding of our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/company/mission-and-values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;value of journalistic independence&lt;/a&gt; and a commitment to our mission to seek the truth and help people understand the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will report to the Engineering Manager, Games App.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years full time experience as a Software Engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of Android-focused experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building user interfaces with complex animations and user interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with Kotlin, including writing unit tests, networking, data persistence and UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated understanding of modern Android technologies such as Jetpack Compose, Coroutines, Hilt/Dagger, and Room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing clean app architectures using modern industry design patterns like MVVM, MVI, or Clean Architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating product goals into quality shippable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledgeable and passionate about AI coding tools especially with mobile development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with backend engineers and understanding of backend architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience dealing with high traffic distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous mobile game development experience running games at scale in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience leading the team and mentoring junior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may require limited on-call hours. An on-call schedule will be determined when you join, taking into account team size and other variables.&lt;/p&gt;
