&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/mission-and-values/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;mission&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; of The New York Times is to seek the truth and help people understand the world. That means independent journalism is at the heart of all we do as a company. It’s why we have a world-renowned newsroom that sends journalists to report on the ground from nearly 160 countries. It’s why we focus deeply on how our readers will experience our journalism, from print to audio to a world-class digital and app destination. And it’s why our business strategy centers on making journalism so good that it’s worth paying for.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Times Opinion is looking for a Senior Producer to lead the original reporting of our enterprise video team. You have experience guiding groundbreaking journalism with an eye for innovation and creative storytelling. You bring a filmmaker’s eye to journalism, pairing cinematic storytelling with a strong understanding of what engages audiences on YouTube and other digital platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond enterprise video journalism, you will help create video guest essays that bring compelling arguments to life. Contributors range from subject-matter experts and public officials to artists, celebrities and ordinary people with extraordinary perspectives. It’s an opportunity to bring fresh voices and bold ideas to our audience, challenging viewers to think differently about the world as it is—and imagine what it could become.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will shape original ideas, make sound editorial decisions and oversee the work of journalists and editors. You will be a trusted resource for colleagues, offering clear editorial guidance and constructive feedback. The ideal candidate thrives in a fast-paced newsroom, helping the team meet deadlines while maintaining high standards of journalism and craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in New York City and requires attendance in the office four days a week. There may be some flexibility to work remotely, subject to departmental guidance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide reporting, approve casting, frame and advance stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edit scripts and re-writes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide notes in edit and rough cut stages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative ideation and visual invention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, critique stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure smooth production with clear deliverables and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide and encourage producers to work to their maximum potential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce original video and experiment with new video formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the work of a team of journalists and creative editors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate support and understanding of our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytco.com/company/mission-and-values/&quot;&gt; value of journalistic independence&lt;/a&gt; and a strong commitment to our mission to seek the truth and help people understand the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will report to our Executive Producer, Opinion Video&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years producing digital news videos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years managing direct reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad knowledge of current events and news&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with digital storytelling formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in the trenches of production, including editing, shooting and field production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writing, editing and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep curiosity about video habits and use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;REQ-019470&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
