&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and maintain plate room equipment, including plate processors, hand jacks, file transmission-related systems, plate lines, and benders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure efficient, productive, and safe work environment by following all department office rules and Standard Operating Procedures&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with team members to maintain positive and productive work relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow production schedules and deadlines to ensure delivery of newspaper editions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lift and carry up to 50 pounds, stand, and walk for 8-10 hours per shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 or more years of experience in a production or warehouse environment in the newspaper production or offset printing industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordination with team members.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work well with people and adapt to changing technology. • High school diploma or equivalency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous newspaper production or offset printing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with plateroom equipment and tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate all equipment during the training period.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a union role represented by the New York Stereotypers #1&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
