&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Publishing group at The New York Times builds and maintains the content management system powering all Times platforms. We empower engineering teams to evolve digital experiences while providing creators with interconnected tools to uphold our journalistic mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Content Data Products team governs the centralized, compliance-cleared platform for all Times content data. Partnering closely with the New AI Products and Platforms (NAPP) team—whose Discovery Engine (search, knowledge graph, and AI) relies on our infrastructure—we ensure our rich archive is ingested, structured, attributed, and indexed across all brands (News, Cooking, Wirecutter, The Athletic, Games) and multimedia formats (articles, video, interactives).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Technical Product Manager II to lead our content data warehouse roadmap and its feeding pipelines. Reporting to the Senior TPM for NAPP, you will partner with engineering to bring product strategy across editorial, AI, and partner requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our New York City headquarters. You can typically expect to come into the office 3 days/week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roadmap Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the strategy and delivery for the content data warehouse and ingestion pipelines for new content types and metadata enrichment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
