&lt;p&gt;4+ years of experience developing technical products as a product manager or in an equivalent role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience partnering with engineering teams and platform users to deliver complex data, cloud infrastructure, developer platform, or other technical products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track record using data and structured reasoning to make product decisions and deliver measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understanding of data infrastructure concepts, including pipelines, compute, storage, data modeling, and governance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience communicating technical concepts, priorities, and tradeoffs to technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background in software development, engineering, data science, or analytics; hands-on experience with data products or platform capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with processing engines such as Spark, Trino, Flink, Kafka, or Airflow, and with lakehouse or cloud data infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with platform migrations, deprecations, vendor evaluations, or infrastructure cost management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with SQL, Python, BigQuery, or Amazon Web Services.&lt;/p&gt;
